# Study S007 — source record: three essays of John D. Cook (a blog, not a paper)
What was read. Three essays on the blog of John
D. Cook (johndcook.com), read in full:
'Categorical models of logics' (2026-10-12);
'Topological models of modal logic' (2026-10-04);
and 'Privacy policies and modal logic'
(2026-10-08) — the essay the first names in its
own related list as 'Modeling policies in modal
logic'. The link posted by Will in MOAT
(2026-11-11) was the first of the three; the
study takes the three together, as the first
essay itself joins them.
What the work is. Cook is a consultant in
applied mathematics, statistics and computing
(the firm is his: Singular Value Consulting, as
his site states); the blog is his long-running
notebook of the mathematics he meets in that
work, and of the data privacy work he names in
the third essay. The three essays are short —
a correspondence table with two footnotes of
precision; a construction with its cases; a
story of the tool of one field taken up
by another. Their matter is the common literature,
named inside them: McKinsey and Tarski for the
topological reading; the Curry-Howard-Lambek
correspondence for the categorical one;
Nissenbaum, and Barth, Datta, Mitchell and
Nissenbaum (2006), for the policies.
# Study S007 — the delta: what the study adds, and what was checked
WHAT IT ADDS (charter rule 6 — only what is new):
Five canonical concepts, cluster S (1.2.171-1.2.175):
a logic read in a category — claims as things,
proofs as ways (1.2.171); Axiom K — the box is a
functor (1.2.172); a logic read in a space — the
box as the interior (1.2.173); the reach of a
family of models (1.2.174); and policies as
modal claims (1.2.175). Four foundations
(1.3.185-1.3.188): category; topology; modal
logic; the tenses. Five words coined and defined
(1.3.189-1.3.193): morphism, functor, coproduct,
intuitionistic, bicartesian.
No canonical scroll is revised. What the study
grounds stands at 23.2.1: the held correspondence
of cluster F (1.2.40) gains its third leg and
stands sharper for it; the standing record
(1.4.x) is read, in synthesis, as a small
category: standing for its things and
receipt-carrying steps for its ways; and the display policy of the warrant
graph of the phextura form is asked, in
synthesis, to be a functor over its edges.
THE ORACLE DOES NOT MOVE (charter rule 12): the
Oracle prices the paper stream, and a study is
not sampled from it. No Novelty Index is taken.
CHECKS RUN (the own receipts of the study):
- The three essays read in full, from their own
